{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"DpopVerifier","roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"code":"DPoP","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" header a caller presented, decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether it proves possession for "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" request and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" access token, and return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the key thumbprint that "},{"code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches against the token’s "},{"code":"cnf.jkt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","text":"Why this lives in the SDK","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guarding an endpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two most often missing: ","type":"text"},{"code":"typ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without pinning it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"dpop+jwt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", any ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"other"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" JWT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by the same key.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"type":"text","text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token"}]},{"type":"text","text":". This enum dispatches on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"embedded key’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"type":"text","text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header says."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"]},{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"]},{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","title":"AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/Request":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" needs to know about the current request.","type":"text"}],"title":"DpopVerifier.Request","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/request","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Request"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" 